# Rank 1975 / CVE-2024-31996 (GHSA-hf43-47q4-fhq5, CWE-94, CWE-95): the
# XWiki escaping tool's `html()` inherits Velocity Tools' HTML-entity
# escaping, which covers `& < > " '` and nothing else
# (xwiki-commons-core/xwiki-commons-velocity/src/main/java/org/xwiki/velocity/tools/EscapeTool.java
# at fix parent b94142e2^):
#
#     public class EscapeTool extends org.apache.velocity.tools.generic.EscapeTool
#     {
#         @Override
#         public String xml(Object content) { ... }   // overridden
#         // no html() override: inherits escapeHtml4, entity-escaping only
#     }
#
# XWiki wiki syntax treats `{{ ... }}` as a macro, so a template answering
# with `$escapetool.html($request.place)` passes the braces through and the
# advisory's PoC ships `{{/html}}{{velocity}}#evaluate($request.eval)` in
# the `place` parameter of `Panels.PanelLayoutUpdate`, closing the enclosing
# HTML macro and evaluating attacker Velocity on the server. Fix b94142e2
# overrides `html()` with a translator that also maps `{` to `&lcub;` and
# `}` to `&rcub;`; the cherry-picks b0805160 (to the 15.5 stream) and
# ed7ff515 (to the 14.10 stream) are its release-branch copies. `git tag
# --contains` puts the fix first in xwiki-commons-15.9-rc-1, then 15.5.4
# and 14.10.19, and the advisory's own maven package record
# (org.xwiki.commons:xwiki-commons-velocity) names exactly those three as
# patched, over the affected ranges >= 3.0.1 < 14.10.19, >= 15.0-rc-1
# < 15.5.4 and >= 15.6-rc-1 < 15.9-rc-1.
#
# The completeness of the escape lives entirely inside the library, so the
# application's `$escapetool.html(...)` call is correct code once the
# library carries the override and identical on both sides of the fix: no
# application-side pattern separates a vulnerable pin from a fixed one, and
# the report that belongs to this CVE is the dependency finding, a Maven
# pin of org.xwiki.commons:xwiki-commons-velocity below 15.9-rc-1. The feed
# holds one threshold per artifact and the advisory's own range has three
# branches, so the patched older-stream micro-releases (14.10.19 onward,
# 15.5.4, 15.5.5) report too, as do pins below the 3.0.1 range floor; that
# is the row's stated residual rather than a second threshold.
#
# Measured on real checkouts of the assigned repository (timeout 180,
# --max-ram 6GB, --cache off, 3 runs per revision): the 15.8 release tree,
# inside the advisory's top affected range, goes 448 -> 450 findings, the
# +2 being VYQL-SCA-001 medium and VYQL-SCA-002 high on
# xwiki-commons-core/xwiki-commons-legacy/xwiki-commons-legacy-velocity/pom.xml,
# both carrying "advisory CVE-2024-31996" and "15.8 is below 15.9-rc-1, the
# first fixed version" (the legacy module declares the coordinate as a real
# dependency at ${project.version}). The 15.9 release tree is clean at 454
# findings, 3/3 runs. The b94142e2^ and b94142e2 development checkouts both
# report 15.9-SNAPSHOT, which the version comparator reads as equal to the
# threshold, so neither fires -- a development tree's version is not the
# released coordinate, and the release-tag pair above is the discriminating
# A/B. Reachability (SCA-002) links through the legacy module's own imports
# of org.xwiki.velocity classes. Platform-family consumers reference the
# coordinate as ${commons.version}, a property no same-tree pom defines, so
# the reader leaves those pins unresolved and they stay silent.
#
# The code-level route stays closed, and the last four tests pin why:
#   - the Java side has no node to bind. At the parent there is no `html()`
#     method in the file at all, so a discriminating binding must key on
#     the *absence of an override* in a subclass of
#     org.apache.velocity.tools.generic.EscapeTool. That is the fixing
#     commit's own layout, and velocity-tools' documentation says nothing
#     that would lead anyone to write it: the genericity test fails, and
#     exactly one such class exists in the world.
#   - the template side is line-regex extraction, not nodes. The
#     xwiki_velocity scope emits input, state_change, csrf_check, escape
#     and wiki_embed events, but the escape event exists only for the
#     `{{{$escapetool` line construct beside the wiki-embed sink; an
#     escape call wrapping a value on an ordinary print line is text
#     inside a matched line, not a node, so "escaped for HTML" and
#     "escaped for wiki syntax" are indistinguishable in the IR. That is
#     the config text-template escape-node engine gap; the final two
#     tests are its isolating pair -- identical template, differing only
#     in the escape. Kinship, not a mint: the same wrong-parser escaping
#     family as code.JavaScriptTemplateHtmlEscapeMismatch (VYQL-INJ-171)
#     and code.ErbHrefUrlHtmlEscapeOnly, and the wiki-render sink half of
#     the pair the xwiki-platform sibling ships for the `{{{$` construct.

test "rank1975: a velocity-tools pin below the first brace-escaping release is a dependency finding"
  lang java
  file src/main/java/example/PanelLayout.java
  code
  ```
  package example;

  import org.apache.velocity.VelocityContext;
  import org.xwiki.velocity.tools.EscapeTool;

  public class PanelLayout {
      private final VelocityContext context = new VelocityContext();

      public PanelLayout()
      {
          this.context.put(EscapeTool.DEFAULT_KEY, new EscapeTool());
      }

      public String place(String requestPlace)
      {
          return new EscapeTool().html(requestPlace);
      }
  }
  ```
  file pom.xml
  code
  ```
  <project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>
    <groupId>example</groupId>
    <artifactId>app</artifactId>
    <version>1.0.0</version>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency>
        <groupId>org.xwiki.commons</groupId>
        <artifactId>xwiki-commons-velocity</artifactId>
        <version>15.8</version>
      </dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </project>
  ```
  expect VYQL-SCA-001
  expect_evidence VYQL-SCA-001 CVE-2024-31996
  expect VYQL-SCA-002

